{"title":"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Solves_for_Floor(x))\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Solves for Floor(x))</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Solves_for_x)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Solves for x)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Solves_for_x)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Solves for x)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(Geometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (Geometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_(by_Art_of_Problem_Solving)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 (by Art of Problem Solving)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd956317ea58c27f04575afc3387696e41cf6b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"45\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, has the property that the sum of all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a95aa4f158b60762ff263f7d5cf9b7be78e872c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor x \\rfloor \\cdot \\{x\\} = a \\cdot x^2\\]\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />\nis <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb2fec2f1cde0059d8eb9c11bcb2bd63142401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/6/06681f5b345750104366c512078960fee8d81b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a512c6943c8bf4d77157cef668f557e0c6f9abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}=x- \\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/170200756543596efeb46fca1cf29a617e8c9192.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def29be326f8e918a820bc3da5e1b1b935751f65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 245 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 593 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 929 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 1331 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 1332$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"461\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Solves_for_Floor.28x.29.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Solves_for_Floor(x))\">Solution 1 (Solves for Floor(x))</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Solves for Floor(x))\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e884a98c06c603f4f9b5e81b057aaea68fdd9144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=\\lfloor x \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba9ae7daf40fad0a8087f3ed6c8094127d30beff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f=\\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> denote the whole part and the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> respectively, for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934ae7841fddf730e524fc6176231d998370f6e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq f&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1553a00c101164a5495321a0abd09e000ea237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=w+f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We rewrite the given equation as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31a339421fd0eecb7a624d2ac0a5f1447bc3e6d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w\\cdot f=a\\cdot(w+f)^2. \\hspace{38.75mm}(1)\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"19\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/9/3199ae094dfeeaade58dacacfe8d3f9948785ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot(w+f)^2\\geq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"19\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536bf62428c3506bfbc8fe401cdea87517c2be19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w\\cdot f\\geq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4712980fe0f544a86a7f7aa64ffaf479536c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w\\geq0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We expand and rearrange <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/92065c69a02d8d1f447af99af24ee3bc79892923.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[af^2+(2a-1)wf+aw^2=0, \\hspace{23mm}(2)\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"19\" /> which is a quadratic with either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7685cc45a97840d46716bca78e46f09104d233b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"10\" /> \n</p><p>For simplicity purposes, we will treat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> as some fixed nonnegative integer so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> is a quadratic with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45e36aab956539c8bfa63f17f6cdbfd85a5e2f4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> By the Quadratic Formula, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4af1dfa281e4a4245bcfe10c49aef3ade00d3168.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f=w\\Biggl(\\frac{1-2a\\pm\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}\\Biggr). \\hspace{25mm}(3)\\]\" width=\"362\" height=\"53\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae8d3e5ff2fa057c1676e487827eacf01181f06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/f/abfed109320342481a4a1877aac28425df3dce6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714adf2c8180edcbb346813de7c32b964a2435c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=w+f=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"118\" height=\"16\" /> which does not affect the sum of the solutions. Therefore, we consider the case for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2faca357cd1888d2e439c35413d92928b857a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w\\geq1:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Recall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bf448584f605b6abfb8c567b40167577bc15969.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq f&lt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1ecf1aab4dae5847f9770fe793799ad6f0506a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-2a\\pm\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}\\geq0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"178\" height=\"40\" /> From the discriminant, we require that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d09694eaf1bbd0dc30634d574528dfd19950f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq1-4a&lt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/7/987273bf5d2d3b2b21ed20a0b523b1b88a1d0dc2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0&lt;a\\leq\\frac14. \\hspace{54mm}(4)\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We consider each part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/4/934ae7841fddf730e524fc6176231d998370f6e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq f&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> separately:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36415c09c1d8ca77e2c0dba21c8cdef4b1056b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /></li><p>\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edfab0dd6bac5131ab929c8459a0de0c4486dd27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d739b6bc9b466142575aa867e6a75af59dad04cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0, (2a-1)w&lt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/0/cd058f6013b6ec182d30f531c31bd262457e3a0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$aw^2&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" /> By Descartes' Rule of Signs, we deduce that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> must have two positive roots, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36415c09c1d8ca77e2c0dba21c8cdef4b1056b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is always valid.</p><p>\nAlternatively, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd745197cba7afe3782047dd959022f1fd297f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> note that all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f092f4f57a68d198985c0c158289845e4abd6b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;a\\leq\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"78\" height=\"37\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/b/ebbd667aa09c5c51ef864ad03b9f33bd357b86fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-2a&gt;\\sqrt{1-4a}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> We deduce that both roots in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> must be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/4/36415c09c1d8ca77e2c0dba21c8cdef4b1056b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is always valid.</p><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2a41af43f0cea9c102c759d512258a2af57654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /></li><p>\nWe rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbf339570471c3d8838277de42d58142e07552f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f=w\\Biggl(\\frac{1}{2a}-1\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}\\Biggr).\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"53\" /> From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd745197cba7afe3782047dd959022f1fd297f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/927563fee6f93ce0fbf75f00cc194db7a9d1716d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2a}\\geq\\frac{1}{1/2}=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"115\" height=\"41\" /> The larger root is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257f3a1d3ffe0009b0b4a96d8d69ee4b0ce9661b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\geq w\\left(2-1+2\\sqrt{1-4a}\\right) \\geq 1\\Biggl(2-1+2\\sqrt{1-4\\cdot\\frac14}\\Biggr) = 1,\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"53\" />\nwhich contradicts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac8c813a951acc76691fd709b973c1cc6ac3f677.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&lt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> So, we take the smaller root, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b15412674320c8cc986e40e743c49bd3ff1119.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f=w\\Biggl(\\frac{1}{2a}-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}\\Biggr)\\]\" width=\"217\" height=\"53\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/3387939d7f97e3f9f95b0bcc1c9b45a4c1d4417f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{1}{2a}-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"216\" height=\"40\" /> We rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95bb29bce38e6381f24cd48ad9d4ec3a1ad8cc40.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f=wk,\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/2/6b2a41af43f0cea9c102c759d512258a2af57654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is valid as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c68fea872f47087d48cd3ea3a5fd978c757c0d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;\\frac 1w.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> Note that the solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are generated at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a8e4f62974958fa290500a704e6bb976af76815.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[w=1,2,3,\\ldots,W,\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" /> up to some value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad46a649e29c666752c74614f626359ecb343102.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff91669888ba0a770750c07f209d8a03c0bd9e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{W+1}\\leq k&lt;\\frac1W.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"140\" height=\"38\" />\n</p></ol>\n<p>Now, we express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddfbb7689d099f701930562aa20ff8d6cf8566b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k:$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e978a042040f4de9ffaf601ddfd537ce956baaab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=w+f=w+wk=w(1+k).\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"18\" />\nThe sum of all solutions to the original equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7c780d69fa818ae798ba64f8d082ee11c0b9a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{w=1}^{W}w(1+k)=(1+k)\\cdot\\sum_{w=1}^{W}w=(1+k)\\cdot\\frac{W(W+1)}{2}=420. \\hspace{10mm}(\\bigstar)\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"51\" />\nAs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86f54d602bd5e561b134d44db7e0406f5abe07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+k&lt;1+\\frac1W,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6edd274b6fbd03a59895030503e167c3c800abc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> is slightly above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56bf90dcb88b860bcced81556a664e182fdcac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{W(W+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"40\" /> is slightly below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2718928887f492262b36045ce7475ba90a0f7027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/75693dd6938adb2cd01a2536cffe4f8e5936931b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W(W+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> is slightly below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/0/4807c1ef12db7e400f09d63ab8a3133989c10ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$840.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> By observations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/6/746f176f0a7a7eab25d6f53ace26802adfea5fde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W=28.$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" /> Substituting this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bf0ed26d362c417a034ab91df4f2f28ad40e272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{1}{29},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> which satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/5/30564a38f0d7b847b1bcdd28f88a8af0e459051f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{W+1}\\leq k&lt;\\frac1W,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" /> as required.\n</p><p>Finally, we solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d68236e488de27ff68d6339c1ea278d633aad671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\frac{1}{2a}-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"188\" height=\"40\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c31f41d4fec95342c44bd1e9ef553393a185b0bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{1}{29}&amp;=\\frac{1}{2a}-1-\\frac{\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a} \\\\ \\frac{2}{29}a&amp;=1-2a-\\sqrt{1-4a} \\\\ \\frac{60}{29}a-1&amp;=-\\sqrt{1-4a} \\\\ \\frac{60^2}{29^2}a^2-\\frac{120}{29}a+1&amp;=1-4a \\\\ \\frac{60^2}{29^2}a^2-\\frac{4}{29}a&amp;=0 \\\\ a\\left(\\frac{60^2}{29^2}a-\\frac{4}{29}\\right)&amp;=0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"307\" height=\"267\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0ef91d683491fed4392ae43db0316ceb2cdbe4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a4795bf70a7208262f83ba1006fc37e6125efac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60^2}{29^2}a-\\frac{4}{29}=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"39\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f41d75e6e61af221b765830d77b76fbf494aeaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a=\\frac{4}{29}\\cdot\\frac{29^2}{60^2}=\\frac{29}{900}.\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"39\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debac7a355de87d03bc414e4ee43e1127b6ea18a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+900=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 929}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"169\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM (inspired by Math Jams's <b>2020 AMC 10/12A Discussion</b>)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Solves_for_x.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Solves_for_x)\">Solution 2 (Solves for x)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Solves for x)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be a root in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d233395e2a6bc75973eebbe2c0966c6d9d201739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n,n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />. In this interval, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf5258c0daa334bafba9de8b2dbdaf5a7adad841.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x_n \\rfloor = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/0093a01dfedcf4a16127ee999398dea2e15887f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_n\\}=x_n-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a62c59d01df0cfb3f4731c98742bb92f6fcad7c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax_n^2 = nx_n-n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"21\" />, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb534420b9f79b6639fd73c44720075a5f61b01c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax_n^2-nx_n+n^2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />. We can homogenize this equation by setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6012ab25e2132eafcc1efcbd0d14510740772f29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=n\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/f/52f583b582db9d2f0ecb3faa89416797da54deac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda38f45a64bbd4451aedeeb4584e01d91239172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5b9053e2c88aac1321f500dd8f8d511d78ac1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\zeta^2-\\zeta+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest integer for which there is such a root; we have, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe88cc71f04ae0063e26e39f9f03ba3a275cb9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,\\ldots , N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d692eaef94e741396b7b39fa48e69f814b190d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n &lt; x_n = n\\zeta &lt; n+1\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" /> Summing over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1edbe71f3508a2f3205debc449b5b943d7e1ddfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\in \\{1,2,\\ldots , N\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21ee4041839f735926f8e8bea8905d209ae648d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tfrac 12 N(N+1) &lt; 420 = \\tfrac 12 N(N+1)\\zeta &lt; \\tfrac 12 N(N+3)\\]\" width=\"373\" height=\"21\" /> From the right inequality we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/d/f2d204b5dfd8815164381b02ed94bb3640193fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27&lt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and from the left one we get  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddc3de9f4d607ebf377296db68080d62744bc30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N&lt;29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4bea29a9620069819683f1e5d6d93797b2d74a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=28$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />. Using this in the middle equality we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e60f72662888fcd77d9fa9d695417c982cd0d0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta = \\tfrac{30}{29}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"53\" height=\"23\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda38f45a64bbd4451aedeeb4584e01d91239172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5b9053e2c88aac1321f500dd8f8d511d78ac1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\zeta^2-\\zeta+1=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/6/ae6dba2869a894f2df21dd36b5d8583c3a4fce3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\zeta^{-2}(\\zeta-1)= \\tfrac{29^2}{30^2}\\cdot \\tfrac 1{29}= \\tfrac{29}{900}.\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"24\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debac7a355de87d03bc414e4ee43e1127b6ea18a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29+900=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 929}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"169\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Shihan\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Solves_for_x.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Solves_for_x)\">Solution 3 (Solves for x)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Solves for x)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd5163623cbb25e453e5d068502db29d0fbf5a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor \\cdot \\{x\\}&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"19\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379056413aa48dec2a4952f1932158caecd19e51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2\\ge 0\\forall x\\in \\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"17\" />. Thus we only need to look at positive solutions (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> doesn't affect the sum of the solutions). \nNext, we break <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e29934842c955ae0d15a48169abc6c8a49c0ac27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor\\cdot \\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"19\" /> down for each interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/39018fd52a875fe699cc282ec9844f1a8370f36a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[n,n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer. Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdb1bbd90bd14cbe97318b65a7c391d4fd3fb79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3aadecf046ed4caf20cf8f3ca4a960fadd37e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x\\}=x-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />. This means that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c9653b5c0d99b6fc846c835d0b0f5c00ded2e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in [n,n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b73e196be5c9238cec5992aed45648cd3c228964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor \\cdot \\{x\\}=n(x-n)=nx-n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"20\" />. Setting this equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762b48c9dabf0dbafca8359fda4f04bea25e3311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax^2$\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7566ffc27f42eafa1ceb9602ff359558709802.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[nx-n^2=ax^2\\implies ax^2-nx+n^2=0 \\implies x=\\frac{n\\pm \\sqrt{n^2-4an^2}}{2a}\\]\" width=\"495\" height=\"40\" />\nWe're looking at the solution with the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340a3179714b30e3a357f098f8c51f443c57f42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{n-n\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}=\\frac{n}{2a}\\left(1-\\sqrt{1-4a}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"312\" height=\"40\" />. Note that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdb1bbd90bd14cbe97318b65a7c391d4fd3fb79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor=n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> is the greatest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e4ebbca9782c9498f9fb737a3352d25eb2c2f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor \\cdot \\{x\\}=ax^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> has a solution, the sum of all these solutions is slightly over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd51b37ba76c6e1b1c8a2e6ce7a6d95010fb1aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n}k=\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"132\" height=\"48\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef6a4dc5b1ee8913137ca5f6c043843d4412af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$406$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6ab729da527d74d526a3c840498ca36eef77f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=28$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, just under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb2fec2f1cde0059d8eb9c11bcb2bd63142401b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$420$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. Checking this gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/75309f9239123b67246e6c3ebddabc6074b62693.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\sum_{k=1}^{28}\\frac{k}{2a}\\left(1-\\sqrt{1-4a}\\right)&amp;=\\frac{1-\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}\\cdot 406=420 \\\\ \\frac{1-\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}&amp;=\\frac{420}{406}=\\frac{30}{29} \\\\ 29-29\\sqrt{1-4a}&amp;=60a \\\\ 29\\sqrt{1-4a}&amp;=29-60a \\\\ 29^2-4\\cdot 29^2a&amp;=29^2+3600a^2-120\\cdot 29a \\\\ 3600a^2&amp;=116a \\\\ a&amp;=\\frac{116}{3600}=\\frac{29}{900} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 929}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"418\" height=\"256\" />\n~ktong\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: Using the Binomial expansion one can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d3e3026294b45a9f2719528eccddf57c2256d14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1-\\sqrt{1-4a}}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"42\" /> is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>~tsun26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050415e17510f6fa427a953038f7064d914904a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\lfloor x \\rfloor \\cdot \\{x\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01ea41c596f3e91b096877425dbe48abb946fe50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=a \\cdot x^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>We make the following table of values:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ae021b2075db17644b3b7694f376e63d2ccab1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|c|c|l} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-2ex] \\boldsymbol{x} &amp; \\boldsymbol{\\lfloor x \\rfloor} &amp; \\boldsymbol{f(x)} &amp; \\multicolumn{1}{c}{\\textbf{Equation}} \\\\ [1.5ex] \\hline &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [-1ex] [0,1) &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; y=0 \\\\ [1.5ex] [1,2) &amp; 1 &amp; [0,1) &amp; y=x-1 \\\\ [1.5ex] [2,3) &amp; 2 &amp; [0,2) &amp; y=2x-4 \\\\ [1.5ex] [3,4) &amp; 3 &amp; [0,3) &amp; y=3x-9 \\\\ [1.5ex] [4,5) &amp; 4 &amp; [0,4) &amp; y=4x-16 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots &amp; \\cdots \\\\ [1.5ex] [m,m+1) &amp; m &amp; [0,m) &amp; y=mx-m^2 \\\\ [1.5ex] \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"264\" />\nWe graph <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> (in red, by branches) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> (in blue, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cdf5e5c4e33271b68b8e1e9316249b80a0fe15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{29}{900}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />) as shown below.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2020_AMC_12A_Problem_25.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/47/2020_AMC_12A_Problem_25.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"578\" height=\"400\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Graph in Desmos: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.desmos.com/calculator/ouvaiqjdzj\">https://www.desmos.com/calculator/ouvaiqjdzj</a>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28Geometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(Geometry)\">Video Solution 1 (Geometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (Geometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This video shows how things like The Pythagorean Theorem and The Law of Sines work together to solve this seemingly algebraic problem: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJ7Jxa98zw&amp;feature=youtu.be\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IJ7Jxa98zw&amp;feature=youtu.be</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xex8TBSzKNE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xex8TBSzKNE</a>\n</p><p>~MathEx\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_3_.28by_Art_of_Problem_Solving.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_(by_Art_of_Problem_Solving)\">Video Solution 3 (by Art of Problem Solving)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 (by Art of Problem Solving)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_mdreGBPvg&amp;t=428s&amp;ab_channel=ArtofProblemSolving\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7_mdreGBPvg&amp;t=428s&amp;ab_channel=ArtofProblemSolving</a>\n</p><p>Created by Richard Rusczyk\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/i5b5P9RPuas\">https://youtu.be/i5b5P9RPuas</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A\">2020 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2020 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017095344\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 848/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2263/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 161/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 28233/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.956      1 -total\n 57.27%    7.420      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 40.37%    5.230      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18141:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017095344 and revision id 293848. Rendering was triggered because: page-edit\n -->\n</div>"}